{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And King Ahasuerus laid a tribute on the land.</b> That which is not under his kingship — only fear of him is upon it, and likewise the islands of the sea that are far from him. And Scripture mentions this to make known that he prospered in all his ways, and his might was seen after Mordecai became second to him."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:26.156398412Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}